86
00:05:12,000 --> 00:05:14,000
This doesn't go away with the season.

87
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:17,000
This is constantly something people are seeking to do.

88
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:22,000
So that's one of the reasons I think lending is one of the more durable businesses in crypto.

89
00:05:22,000 --> 00:05:24,000
And we can dive all into the different types of lending,

90
00:05:24,000 --> 00:05:26,000
but that's what makes it interesting.

91
00:05:26,000 --> 00:05:30,000
With the TVL drop off, I think this cuts into a recent trend that we've seen,

92
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:35,000
which is the forms of lending and borrowing to use cases that we see on chain

93
00:05:35,000 --> 00:05:39,000
have completely changed over the past year to two years.

94
00:05:39,000 --> 00:05:42,000
So originally, if you look at what lending started as,

95
00:05:42,000 --> 00:05:44,000
it started as CDPs where you would put up money

96
00:05:44,000 --> 00:05:47,000
and you would get a synthetic dollar essentially against this.

97
00:05:47,000 --> 00:05:49,000
I'm going to roll you back for a second.

